{"id": "EUVD-2026-97666", "enisaUuid": "96674712-bb31-3176-b813-3ab89407e805", "description": "Zebra 2.3.0 before 6.4.0 contains a protection mechanism failure that allows unauthenticated peers to evade bans because bans and misbehavior scores are keyed on exact IP addresses. Attackers can reconnect from fresh IPv6 addresses in their /64 allocation or flush the 20,000-entry FIFO ban list to restore access for banned peers.", "datePublished": "2026-10-12T16:05:42", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-13T16:53:12", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/ZcashFoundation/zebra/security/advisories/GHSA-jhpp-8h75-7pv5", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/zebra-2.3.0-before-6.4.0-peer-ban-bypass-via-exact-ip-keying"], "aliases": ["GHSA-vw8x-hqvx-7q8q", "CVE-2026-109364"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.24, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "8ac19940-726b-37c6-9944-6f4dba44dd2f", "product": {"name": "zebra", "vendor": {"name": "ZcashFoundation"}}, "product_version": "2.3.0 <6.4.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "c4549c70-003b-3522-b65c-db04e250d810", "vendor": {"name": "ZcashFoundation"}}], "isExploited": false}